# Manually transcribed by OWID from a Census of Canada report giving the share of children aged
# 10-13 who were 'gainfully occupied' in the 1921 and 1931 censuses, by sex.
# NOTE: the exact census volume and table for these figures still needs to be confirmed; the
# citation below is provisional.
# In case of updating, upload manually.

# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Census of Canada: children gainfully occupied, 1921 and 1931"
    description: |-
      Rates published in a Census of Canada report, giving the share of children aged 10-13 who were recorded as 'gainfully occupied' in the 1921 and 1931 censuses, separately for boys and girls.

      'Gainfully occupied' counts only children working for money or its equivalent, so unpaid work on the family farm is excluded. This is a narrower concept than the occupational counts of the 1891 census, in which most of the recorded boys were farmers' sons.
    date_published: "1931"

    # Citation
    producer: Dominion Bureau of Statistics
    citation_full: |-
      Dominion Bureau of Statistics. Census of Canada, 1931. Children aged 10-13 gainfully occupied, 1921 and 1931. Ottawa.
    attribution_short: Census of Canada

    # Files
    url_main: https://www12.statcan.gc.ca/History/Index-eng.cfm
    date_accessed: '2026-09-06'

